\begin{abstract}
The design spectrum of a simple graph $G$ is the set of positive integers $n$ such that there exists an edgewise
decomposition of the complete graph $K_n$ into $n(n - 1)/(2 |E(G)|)$ copies of $G$.
We compute the design spectra for 7788 6-regular graphs with 12 vertices.
\end{abstract}

