Rejected after full-paper and implementation audit: no defensible family clears H.

- [REJECTED.md](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2401.02846/REJECTED.md) documents the Track A and Track B failures, citing Sections 1, 4, 6, Lemma 4.7, and Theorem 5.1 of the [paper](https://arxiv.org/abs/2401.02846).
- The implementation is preserved as [rejected_gen_2401_02846.py](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2401.02846/rejected_gen_2401_02846.py).
- [selftest_report.json](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2401.02846/selftest_report.json) records the corrected baseline.

The decisive measurement was 823 operations per instance for the honest mechanical attack versus 221 for the proposed shortcut—only a 3.7× difference, with both performing essentially the same quadratic marked-difference search. Thus Track B fails; the paper supplies no distributional hardness theorem supporting Track A. G and V did pass.

The previous oracle transcripts were retained, but contain only HTTP 403 quota errors and provide no hardness evidence.
